; 128K: page in bank 0 with ROM 1
;
; Writes $10 to port $7FFD: RAM bank 0 at $C000, ROM 1, normal screen, which is the paging state of the game. The 128K
; hooks use it as the return address of a call into the music bank (#R$85C2); the start-up code (#R$6000) calls it on
; every machine, where on a 48K Spectrum it does nothing visible.
; .
; Hardware: writes the 128K paging port $7FFD (through #R$85CA).
;
; O:A $10, the value written
@label=PageInBank0
@isub=LD A,PAGING_BANK0
c$85BE LD A,$10
 $85C0 JR $85CA
